This suite tests whether headers have the declarations of the Single UNIX
Specification, Version 2 (UNIX 98, _XOPEN_SOURCE 500) that later editions
removed.

It is V86BSD's, not os-test's (see ../README.V86BSD).  The tests are made
by ../legacy/gen.sh from the .api files in ../legacy, which were written
by hand from the text of the editions; each test is marked with the last
edition that had the declaration (SUSv2, SUSv3 or SUSv4), and where the
declaration changed between editions, it is the last one's.  They are
compiled with -D_XOPEN_SOURCE=500 (../misc/try-compile-legacy.sh): a
declaration that a system has only with its own feature macros
(_DEFAULT_SOURCE, _GNU_SOURCE ...) is an "extension".
